\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. There's a friend for little children
\par Above the bright blue sky,
\par A friend who never changeth,
\par Whose love can never die.
\par Unlike our friends by nature,
\par Who change with changing years,
\par This Friend is always worthy 
\par The precious name He bears.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. There's a home for little children
\par Above the bright blue sky,
\par Where Jesus reigns in glory,
\par A home of peace and joy.
\par No home on earth is like it,
\par Or can with it compare;
\par For every one is happy,
\par Nor could be happier, there.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. There's a song for little children
\par Above the bright blue sky,
\par A song that will not weary
\par Though sung continually,
\par A song which even angels
\par Can never, never sing;
\par They know not Christ as Saviour,
\par But worship Him as King.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. There's a robe for little children
\par Above the bright blue sky,
\par And a harp of sweetest music,
\par And a palm  of victory.
\par All, all above is treasured,
\par And found in Christ alone;
\par O come, dear little children,
\par That all may be your own.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

